==============================================================================
CLAIM A3 -- WHY it can never fire: str.lower() cannot emit an ASCII capital
==============================================================================
Exhaustive over the entire Unicode codepoint range, so this is a proof and not a sample.

  codepoints whose .lower() contains ASCII 'Q'               : []
  codepoints whose .lower() contains ANY char of 'QUESTION'  : []
  multi-char lowerings still containing an ASCII capital     : []
  codepoints where .lower() is NOT idempotent                : []
  Greek final-sigma context rule: 'OΔOΣ'.lower() -> 'ΟΔΟΣ' -> 'οδος'

  VERDICT A3: 'no input can put a capital Q past line 25' -> PROVED

==============================================================================
CLAIM A -- CONTROL: do the SIBLING guards on lines 29/30 fire?
==============================================================================
If they did not either, the defect would be 'the whole tail is dead', not 'line 31'.

  preprocess_output('kitchen <CONTEXT> blah'          ) = 'kitchen '
  preprocess_output('kitchen <EXAMPLE> blah'          ) = 'kitchen '
  preprocess_output('kitchen <context> blah'          ) = 'kitchen '
  preprocess_output('kitchen Question: blah'          ) = 'kitchen question: blah'

  CONTROL PASSED: 29/30 fire on their lowercase literals, 31 does not fire on its capitalised one.

